<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-8">8 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson defeats the British at New Orleans</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Jackson's mixed force repulsed a British assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, inflicting some 2,000 casualties. Fought after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ghent">Treaty of Ghent</a> was signed but before news arrived, it made Jackson a national hero.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-26">26 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon escapes from Elba</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">With about a thousand men, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> slipped away from his island exile and sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He regained power without a shot, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a> that ended at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-1">1 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon lands in France after escaping Elba</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> came ashore at Golfe-Juan near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannes">Cannes</a> with about a thousand men. Troops sent to stop him joined him instead, and he entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 20 March to begin the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-20">20 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon returns to Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xviii">Louis XVIII</a> fled, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> entered the Tuileries to cheering crowds. His restored rule, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>, ended with defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> in June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-10">10 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount Tambora reaches its cataclysmic climax</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Indonesian volcano produced the largest eruption in recorded history, killing tens of thousands on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a>. Its ash cooled the globe, making 1816 the 'Year Without a Summer'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tolentino" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tolentino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-3">3 May</a> · Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tolentino">Battle of Tolentino</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tolentino was fought on 2–3 May 1815 near Tolentino in the Marche, Italy, between Joachim Murat's Neapolitan army and the Austrians.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-9">9 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Congress of Vienna signs its Final Act</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Days before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>, the great powers signed the treaty redrawing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s map after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Its settlement shaped European borders and diplomacy for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-16">16 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon defeats Blücher's Prussians at Ligny</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s Armée du Nord defeated part of a Prussian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a> at Ligny, while Ney held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a> at Quatre Bras. The bulk of the Prussian army survived and fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> two days later; Ligny was Napoleon's last victory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-quatre-bras">Quatre Bras</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-18">18 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Wellington and Blücher defeat Napoleon at Waterloo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a>'s Prussians broke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s final assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>'s army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>. Napoleon abdicated four days later and was exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-15">15 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon surrenders aboard HMS Bellerophon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Unable to escape to America, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> gave himself up to Captain Frederick Maitland of HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellerophon">Bellerophon</a> off Rochefort. The British exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">Saint Helena</a>, where he died in 1821.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamestown.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-15">15 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon arrives in exile at Saint Helena</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a> anchored off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">Saint Helena</a>, carrying the defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. On this remote South Atlantic island he spent his last six years, dying there in 1821.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-7">7 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Marshal Ney is executed by firing squad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michel-ney">Michel Ney</a>, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> called 'the bravest of the brave', was shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> for treason after joining his former emperor during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>. He refused a blindfold and is said to have given the order to fire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-23">23 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Jane Austen's Emma is published</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">John Murray published Emma, though its title page bore the date 1816. Austen's comedy of a confident young matchmaker is often judged her most accomplished novel.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1815">Treaty of Paris (1815)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Paris of November 1815 was signed after Napoleon's defeat at Waterloo and his Hundred Days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention">Kandyan Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kandyan Convention was the agreement signed on 2 March 1815 between the British and the chiefs of the Kingdom of Kandy, after they had helped the British depose King Sri Vikrama Rajasinha.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-white-terror" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-white-terror.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-white-terror">Second White Terror</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Second White Terror was a wave of royalist reprisals in southern France in 1815, after Napoleon's Hundred Days and the second restoration of Louis XVIII.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-pi">Battle of Fei Pi</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Fei Pi was fought on Tahiti in November 1815 between Pōmare II, returning from exile on Moorea, and the chiefs opposed to him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-oriente">Congress of Oriente</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress of Oriente was an assembly of the Federal League convened by José Gervasio Artigas at Arroyo de la China, now Concepción del Uruguay, in June 1815.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/neapolitan-war">Neapolitan War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Neapolitan War was fought in 1815 between the Kingdom of Naples under Joachim Murat and the Austrian Empire.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-seventh-coalition" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-seventh-coalition.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-seventh-coalition">War of the Seventh Coalition</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The War of the Seventh Coalition was the final campaign of the Napoleonic Wars, fought in 1815 after Napoleon escaped from Elba and retook power in France during the Hundred Days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/german-federal-act">German Federal Act</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The German Federal Act of 8 June 1815 was the founding treaty of the German Confederation, agreed at the Congress of Vienna and incorporated into its Final Act.</p></div></li></ol></section>
