<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress of Vienna grants Prussia the Rhineland and Westphalia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom%20of%20Great%20Britain%20and%20Ireland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wellington and Blücher defeat Napoleon at Waterloo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/swiss-confederation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swiss%20Confederation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swiss Confederation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The great powers recognise Switzerland's perpetual neutrality</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Luxembourg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Luxembourg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress of Vienna creates the grand duchy under William I of the Netherlands</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-confederation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Confederation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Confederation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Federal Act creates the German Confederation at the Congress of Vienna</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nguyen%20dynasty.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nguyen dynasty</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Gia Long Code, modelled on Qing law, is issued</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-tahiti"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Tahiti.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Tahiti</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pōmare II defeats the chiefs of the old religion at the Battle of Fei Pi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/napoleon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Napoleon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Napoleon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Escaping from exile on Elba, he retakes power for the Hundred Days, is defeated at Waterloo and is sent to Saint Helena</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/simon-bolivar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sim%C3%B3n%20Bol%C3%ADvar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Simón Bolívar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He resigns his command in New Granada, sails into exile on Jamaica and writes the Jamaica Letter</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/congress-poland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Congress%20Poland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Congress Poland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress of Vienna creates the Kingdom of Poland from most of the Duchy of Warsaw, ruled by Tsar Alexander I</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/otto-von-bismarck"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Otto%20von%20Bismarck.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Otto von Bismarck</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Born at Schönhausen, a noble family estate west of Berlin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The powers at the Congress of Vienna declare Napoleon an outlaw and the United Kingdom, Russia, Austria and Prussia mobilise armies against him</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The French cross the frontier near Charleroi before dawn on 15 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Napoleon defeats the Prussians at Ligny while Ney fights Wellington's forces at Quatre Bras on 16 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wellington withdraws to the ridge of Mont-Saint-Jean and the Prussians fall back to Wavre on 17 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Anglo-allied army holds the ridge against French attacks from late morning until the Imperial Guard is repulsed at about 19:30</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wellington and Blücher meet near La Belle Alliance at around 21:00 and the Prussians pursue the French through the night</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Napoleon announces his second abdication on 24 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-waterloo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Waterloo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Waterloo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Napoleon surrenders to Captain Frederick Maitland of HMS Bellerophon on 15 July, and is later exiled to Saint Helena</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/new-orleans"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Orleans.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Orleans</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Andrew Jackson's forces defeat the British at the Battle of New Orleans</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/ishtar-gate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ishtar%20Gate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ishtar Gate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Claudius Rich's topographical records of the ruins of Babylon, the first ever published, appeared</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pacifism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pacifism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pacifism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The New York Peace Society is founded, and the London Peace Society follows in 1816</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-slavism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Slavism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Slavism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Napoleonic Wars end, and the Pan-Slavism movement begins to grow rapidly</span></li></ul></section>
